OL,3,AA beautiful Himalayan bird is changing
OL,4,Aits voice due to human activity,
OL,5,Aresearch shows
OL,6,
OL,7,FA sharp increase in human activity is
OL,8,Fhaving an impact on the way a Himalayan
OL,9,Fbird lives and communicates, two
OL,10,Fstudies by Indian researchers have
OL,11,Ffound.
OL,13,FThe monal, a pheasant native to
OL,14,FHimalayan mountain forests, is deeply
OL,15,Fwoven into the region's cultural,
OL,16,Ffolklore and identity. The eye-catching
OL,17,Fmonal - the male has distinctive green,
OL,18,Fblue and copper feathers - is the state
OL,19,Fbird of India's Uttarakhand state and
OL,20,Fthe national bird of Nepal, reflecting
OL,21,Fits cultural significance across the
OL,22,FHimalayas.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11914
SC,0014
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1791350369
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AA beautiful Himalayan bird is changing
OL,4,Aits voice due to human activity,
OL,5,Aresearch shows
OL,6,
OL,7,FBut studies show that infrastructure
OL,8,Fdevelopment and tourism are squeezing
OL,9,Fits habitat, while increasing noise is
OL,10,Faltering how it communicates with
OL,11,Fpotential mates and rivals.
OL,13,FResearchers from Uttarakhand conducted
OL,14,Ftwo separate studies over five years
OL,15,Fwhich flagged key threats to the bird.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/39
